        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So ['mini.visits'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/readmes/mini-visits.md) is a released thing now. It has the functionality to persistently add labels to paths and [later reuse them](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cc3a220ecc27d56a7023f1592e14d46a86cd729/doc/mini-visits.txt#L264-L286). I think this will be the recommended way of utilizing the suggested \"marks\" workflow.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned (for 'mini.files').",
